option.SHADOW_BLUENESS=Shadow blueness
option.shadowDistance=Shadow distance
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow resolution
option.shadowIntervalSize=Shadow refocus §e[?]
option.shadowIntervalSize.comment=Determines after how many blocks shadows refocus on the player
option.entityShadowDistanceMul=Entity shadow range §e[?]
option.entityShadowDistanceMul.comment=As a percentage of shadow distance
option.SHADOW_PIXEL=Shadow pixelization
option.HDR=HDR highlights §e[?]
option.HDR.comment=Keeps light brighter than white instead of clipping it: glowing texels, flames and strongly lit surfaces roll off toward white (hot cores) instead of flattening to one color. Everything below white is unchanged
option.LIGHT_CONTRAST=Light contrast §e[?]
option.LIGHT_CONTRAST.comment=Separates light levels a little more: darker caves, shade and nights, block light that pools around its source with a brighter core, and deeper sun shadows. Bright sunlit surfaces are untouched. 0 = original look
option.LIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Sun brightness
option.sunPathRotation=Sun path angle §e[!]
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Miniature was designed with straight shadows in mind and may produce artifacts if changed
option.SHADOW_DARKNESS=Shadow darkness
option.FLAT_LIGHTING=Flat lighting §e[?]
option.FLAT_LIGHTING.comment=Without flat lighting, blocks will have shadows that do not match the sun's position, like in vanilla
option.ENABLE_SHADOWS=Enable shadows
option.SHADOW_ENTITY=Entity shadows
value.SHADOW_ENTITY.-1=§aOff
value.SHADOW_ENTITY.0=§ePlayer
value.SHADOW_ENTITY.1=§eAll

screen.REFLECTIONS_SCREEN=Reflections
option.REFLECTIONS=Reflection opacity
option.BLOCK_REFLECTIONS=Block reflections §e[?]
option.BLOCK_REFLECTIONS.comment=Adds reflections to blocks such as stone bricks, quartz, etc.
option.SSR_MAX_STEPS=Maximum steps
option.SSR_BINARY_STEPS=Refining steps
option.SSR_STEP_SIZE=Step size

screen.BLOOM_SCREEN=Glow
option.BLOOM=Enable glow
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Glow strength
option.BLOOM_HALO_SIZE=Glow size §e[?]
option.BLOOM_HALO_SIZE.comment=How far the glow spreads around light sources. 0 keeps only a tight glow hugging the source; 1 is the default soft halo; higher values give a wide, Photon-like bloom
option.BLOOM_QUALITY=Glow quality §e[?]
option.BLOOM_QUALITY.comment=Fast blurs at quarter resolution with fewer samples; Fancy uses more samples for smoother glow
value.BLOOM_QUALITY.0=§aFast
value.BLOOM_QUALITY.1=§eBalanced
value.BLOOM_QUALITY.2=§cFancy
option.BLOOM_SATURATION=Glow saturation §e[?]
option.BLOOM_SATURATION.comment=Above 1 makes the glow color more vivid than the source texture; below 1 washes it out
option.BLOOM_SKY=Sky glow §e[?]
option.BLOOM_SKY.comment=Lets the sun and bright sky glow; blocks are unaffected - they glow only through real light emission
option.BLOOM_PIXEL_THRESHOLD=Glow pixel cutoff §e[?]
option.BLOOM_PIXEL_THRESHOLD.comment=Base brightness a pixel of a light-emitting block needs to glow. Flame-bodied blocks (lantern, campfire, torch) use a stricter value, lava and glowstone a lower one. Raise if block bodies glow, lower if flames lose glow
option.BLOOM_EMISSIVE_TEXTURES=Pack emissives §e[?]
option.BLOOM_EMISSIVE_TEXTURES.comment=Adds glow to emissive overlay textures from resource packs (rendered fullbright)
option.BLOOM_PARTICLES=Particle glow §e[?]
option.BLOOM_PARTICLES.comment=Bright particles (fire, flames, lava drips) glow. The beacon beam has its own dedicated glow, always on with Glow enabled
screen.COLORED_LIGHT_SCREEN=Colored light
option.COLORED_LIGHT=Colored lighting §e[?]
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Real colored block light: every light source spreads its own color through a light volume around you, at its real vanilla light level. Light flows around corners and through doorways, is tinted by stained glass, never passes through walls, and colors from several sources mix. Iris only, all dimensions
option.COLORED_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Color intensity §e[?]
option.COLORED_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Saturation of the light colors: higher values deepen the hues, lower values keep them subtle. Brightness is unaffected
option.CL_ENTITY_LIGHT=Entity lights §e[?]
option.CL_ENTITY_LIGHT.comment=Light items held by other players and mobs emit colored light, burning entities and flaming arrows glow warm, and blazes, magma cubes, glow squids and allays emit their own light. Requires Entity shadows set to All (Shadows screen)
option.CL_ITEM_LIGHT=Item lights §e[?]
option.CL_ITEM_LIGHT.comment=Dropped light items and item frames holding one (torch, lantern, glowstone...) emit colored light. Requires Entity shadows set to All (Shadows screen)
option.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE=Light color range §e[?]
option.COLORED_LIGHT_RANGE.comment=Horizontal distance (in blocks) up to which colored light replaces plain vanilla block light; it fades back to vanilla beyond. Automatically capped at half the Volume size
option.VOXEL_SIZE=Volume size §e[?]
option.VOXEL_SIZE.comment=Width of the colored light volume in blocks, centered on you; height doubles past 256. Blocks are only known inside the Shadow distance, so keep the Volume within about twice the Shadow distance. GPU memory and compute cost grow with the square of this value: 64-128 cheap, 256 moderate, 384-512 heavy
option.TORCH_FALLOFF=Light softness §e[?]
option.TORCH_FALLOFF.comment=Reshapes the vanilla block light curve: above 1 lifts dark corners and smooths the hard distance steps of torch light (works everywhere, no leaking possible); below 1 makes falloff harsher. 1.0 = vanilla curve
option.CL_LAVA_TEXTURE=Lava texture color §e[?]
option.CL_LAVA_TEXTURE.comment=Lava and magma take their light color from the resource pack (biome tint or texture) instead of the Lava & magma palette sliders. Off = fixed palette color
option.CL_FALLOFF=Light reach §e[?]
option.CL_FALLOFF.comment=How far colored light carries. The lowest value matches vanilla reach (a level-15 source fades out after about 15 blocks); higher values carry the light and its color farther. Brightness close to the source does not change

